      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Adding my feedback into this again as I'm also having severe flickering/highlighting issues with specular highlights still.\n\nEasy steps to reproduce without external assets:\n\n1. Create a new avatar using the VRC Avatar SDK Robot Avatar Example\n\n2. Create a new Material, selecting Toon Standard and apply it to both material slots\n\n3. Enable the specular tab and leave everything else at default.\n\n5. Upload avatar\n\n6. Easiest to see in dark environments with contrasting light elements and baked reflection probes. The example I'm using is wrld_02e1feb9-f2d2-483b-89cf-b9f6bf23bf33\n\nI do also want to specify that this behavior is still happening even for materials that do have a gloss map specified in SDK 3.8.1\n\nEdit: Alright, after unhealthy amounts of perseverance, I've managed to find a solution and likely culprit. Having 'Use Normal Map' enabled seemingly resolves the issue; even without having any actual normal map applied. Guessing it's some sort of math issue in the specular model.",
